app,backend,before_window,after_window,before_minimum,after_minimum,note
app,backend,修改前視窗,修改後視窗,修改前最小,修改後最小,備註
P5,appkit,480x408,551x408,120x121,551x166,"WIDTH GREW 480 -> 551. The window is max(minimum, proposed) and the proposal is .defaultSize 480x380, so a minimum width of 551 now sets the width. Height unchanged."
P50,appkit,780x928,780x928,82x374,299x434,"Minimum width 82 -> 299 and minimum height 374 -> 434, but both stay under the 780x900 proposal, so the window is unchanged on both axes."
P52,appkit,1000x928,1000x928,724x0,724x0,"Unchanged in every number. Its buttons are one character wide, so neither Button change moves anything here."
P5,uikit,n/a,n/a,n/a,n/a,"A phone window cannot grow, so the width shows up as layout: the three alert buttons used to wrap to two lines each and fit inside the 440-point window; now each label is one line, the row is wider than the window and CLIPPED at both edges (-lert A ... Show Alert C (stacks o-). Captures p5-ios-final-20260918-082215.png (before) and -081830.png (after)."
P50,uikit,n/a,n/a,n/a,n/a,"Pixel-identical before and after apart from the status bar clock and the home indicator: changed rows are y 80..130 and y 2832..2840 only. Captures -082312.png and -081959.png."
P52,uikit,n/a,n/a,n/a,n/a,"Pixel-identical on the same test as P50. Captures -082410.png and -082059.png."
P36,appkit,820x728,820x728,279x466,279x481,"Checked because WinUI grew here (822x732 -> 822x797). On AppKit it does not: the minimum height rises 466 -> 481, which is the buttons no longer collapsing, but it stays far under the 820x700 proposal so the window is identical. The difference between the two backends is whether that app window was already sitting at its minimum."
